vars:pre-request {
  eventId: 460e138d-d11c-4e6b-a65e-570b093ec809
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  ## One slot or many
  `slots` accepts **1 to 50** timeline slots. Only the first slot is required -
  every additional slot is optional, so a single payload is enough:

  ```json
  {
    "slots": {
      "startTime": "2026-05-15T09:00:00.000Z",
      "endTime": "2026-05-15T10:00:00.000Z",
      "title": "Stage Setup"
    }
  }
  ```

  The array form works as before - `{"slots": [ { ... }, { ... } ]}`. An empty
  array is rejected with `slots must contain at least one timeline slot`.

  `startTime`, `endTime` and `title` are required per slot. `description`,
  `priority` (defaults to `MEDIUM`), `dependencies`, `assignedTo`, `assignees`
  and `taskId` are optional. `taskId` must be a task of **this** event - a task
  from another event is rejected with
  `One or more taskIds do not exist or do not belong to this event`. The same
  task may be linked to more than one slot.
}

